      "title": "IAM Engineer - Software Engineer - Privileged Access Management - Senior Consultant - SDC",
      "company": "EY",
      "url": "https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Ey",
      "linkedin_url": "",
      "location": "Dallas, TX, USA",
      "description": "Location: Dallas\n\nOther locations: Primary Location Only\n\nSalary: Competitive\n\nDate: Nov 21, 2026\n\n**Job description**\n-------------------\n\nRequisition ID: 1762993\n\nAt EY, we\u2019re all in to shape your future with confidence.\n\n  \n\nWe\u2019ll help you succeed in a globally connected powerhouse of diverse teams and take your career wherever you want it to go. Join EY and help to build a better working world.\n\n  \n\n**About the Role**\n\nWe are seeking a Software Engineer to join our Dallas Service Delivery Center (SDC) and design, develop, deploy, and support services that automate privileged-access workflows. This role will build API- and event-driven solutions for privileged-account onboarding, vaulting, validation, membership management, and self-service capabilities across CyberArk, Delinea Server Suite, HashiCorp Vault, and related platforms.\n\n  \n\n**Key Responsibilities**\n\n* Design, develop, deploy, and support secure backend APIs, connectors, and workflow services that automate privileged-account onboarding, vaulting, lifecycle actions, role membership, and related PAM capabilities.\n* Develop resilient integrations using REST APIs, Microsoft Graph, Azure Service Bus, microservices, event-driven architecture, queue processing, and PAM platform integrations.\n* Translate business and technical requirements into solution designs, API contracts, user stories, test scenarios, and production-ready code.\n* Implement secure development and automated testing practices, including unit, integration, API, end-to-end, regression, disaster-recovery, secrets management, code-quality, and least-privilege controls.\n* Build and maintain CI/CD and deployment processes while troubleshooting application, API, queue, integration, data, and deployment issues using observability, resiliency, retry, and error-handling patterns.\n* Collaborate across product, architecture, UX, DevOps, PAM, infrastructure, and engineering teams through Agile planning, design and code reviews, testing, release readiness",
